Section: Fauxberry Request to Claude 3.5

# 1. Initialize variables
Let the task be set to "Explain how quantum entanglement works."
Let conversation history be an empty list.
Let api_key be "your_anthropic_api_key".

# 2. Define a function to send a message to Claude via the API
To send message to Claude with model "claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022", using message content:
    Make an HTTP POST request to "https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages".
    Set headers to:
        x-api-key as api_key,
        anthropic-version as "2023-06-01",
        content-type as "application/json".
    
    Set the body of the request to:
    ```
    {
        "model": "claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022",
        "max_tokens": 8182,
        "system": "<TASK>\n${task}\n\n<INSTRUCTIONS>\nSlow down your thinking by breaking complex questions into multiple reasoning steps.\nEach individual reasoning step should be brief.\nReturn <DONE> after the last step.",
        "messages": [
            {"role": "user", "content": "Think about your next reasoning step to perform the TASK. Return just the next step."},
            ... reasoning steps
        ]
    }
    ```

    Return the response from Claude.

# 3. Define Fauxberry thinking loop
To start thinking loop for the task:
    Let continue_loop be true.
    
    While continue_loop is true:
        # 4. Add the message asking for the next reasoning step
        Add "Think about your next reasoning step to perform the TASK. Return just the next step." to conversation history.

        # 5. Send the current message to Claude
        Let response be the result of calling "send message to Claude" with the last item in conversation history.
        
        # 6. Add the response to the conversation history
        Add response to conversation history.
        
        # 7. Check if Claude has finished reasoning (looks for <DONE> tag)
        If the response contains "<DONE>":
            Set continue_loop to false.

# 8. Final task completion request
To complete the task:
    # 9. After the <DONE> tag is detected, request the final output
    Add "Complete the <TASK>. Do not return <DONE>." to conversation history.
    
    # 10. Send the request to Claude for the final output
    Let final_response be the result of calling "send message to Claude" with the last item in conversation history.
    
    # 11. Display the final response
    Display final_response.

# 12. Start the Fauxberry thinking loop and complete the task
Start thinking loop for the task.
Complete the task.
